        {
          "id": "krea2-48bf71da72c67ced0b00a95a",
          "alias": "单女围巾雪地忧伤倚靠泼洒",
          "prompt": "The rugged fabric texture and tassel edges on the scarf peek out in the snow, warm and full of life. The clash of red and gray in the cold snowy scene only adds a sense of restrained romance and resilience; The foreground features dense drifting snowflakes, pouring down diagonally from above the frame. Some snowflakes are blurred into hazy light spots in front of the frame, creating a strong sense of depth and spatial layering. The middle ground is the area from the woman's head to her shoulders, where the snowflakes are densest, the figure outlines clear, and the emotions are fully expressed. The background is completely blurred into a dark, blurred shadow of trees or building silhouettes, with only faint branch shapes and dark green tones recognizable. This minimalist background treatment not only enhances the prominence of the subject but also gives the painting a cinematic narrative atmosphere and aesthetic of blank space; The entire composition uses close-ups, with a slightly upward angle to make the characters more approachable and emotionally moving. The main subject is positioned slightly to the left of the center, while the right side has breathing space, creating a visually balanced and natural visual effect; In terms of lighting, backlighting or side backlighting techniques are used, with the overall tone leaning toward a mix of warm brown and low-saturation cool gray, creating a nostalgic atmosphere reminiscent of a retro film filter. Snow particles show faint highlights under the light, enhancing the image's realism and dreamlike feel. The overall atmosphere is filled with a quiet, contemplative, gentle, and slightly lonely poetic quality, as if time has frozen in this moment, with only snowflakes silently falling, witnessing a gentle moment blooming alone in a cold world. It carries a strong artistic film texture and a sense of everyday authenticity, like street photography taken at dusk with an old-fashioned digital camera. The noise is slight but rich in film graininess, with slightly defocused edges adding a touch of haziness and the beauty of time.",
