        {
          "id": "krea2-ef2844dd7cd2f370ecc9d5f6",
          "alias": "单女和服森林愤怒站立泼洒",
          "prompt": "deep within a forest covered with autumn maple leaves, a woman dressed in traditional kimono stands quietly at the lower center of the frame. She stands with her back to the camera, her figure slender and elegant, her robes flowing like clouds. The white base is dotted with deep ink-colored floral patterns, creating a strong and harmonious visual contrast with the surrounding fiery red-orange tones; Her right hand gently holds a pale purple paper umbrella, its edge tinged with delicate dark patterns, the ribs clearly visible, and the surface slightly tilted, as if trying to block or catch the gentle light pouring down from above; Her posture is low and humble, her head slightly tilted, as if gazing at the path paved with withered leaves beneath her feet, or deep in thought, infusing the entire painting with a touch of tranquility, restraint, and poetic Eastern aesthetics; In the foreground is a thick carpet of fallen leaves interwoven with golden yellow and ochre colors. The leaf edges are slightly scorched and clear, with some leaves naturally curling due to gravity, glowing with a warm golden sheen under soft light. These layers cover the ground, creating a rich sense of seasonal and tactile layers; In the middle are several tall and upright maple trees, with thick, dark trunks and twisted branches that stretch upward, forming a natural frame structure. One of the trees stands behind the woman, its branches interwoven like black silhouettes among the brilliant sea of leaves, enhancing the sense of spatial depth in the painting; The background is a continuous, fiery maple forest, with leaves transitioning from bright orange-red to deep burgundy and then to gray-purple from near to far. The colors are highly saturated, as if the entire sky is dyed with flames. In the distance, the mist-shrouded outlines of mountains can be faintly seen, adding a hazy poetic touch and a sense of spatial extension to the scene. The composition adopts a classic vertical style, with trees as vertical guiding lines running through the painting, cleverly placing the figures below the visual center to form a stable and dynamic triangular structure. At the same time, the spatial layout of fallen leaves in the foreground, tree trunks in the center, and maple forests in the background is layered to enhance the depth and richness of perspective. The visual guide line starts from the tip of the paper umbrella held by the figure, naturally extends down along the curve of their body to the fallen leaves beneath their feet, then converges upward along the diagonal lines of the tree trunk to the sky, finally leading to distant mountains and horizons, allowing the viewer's gaze to roam freely and immerse themselves in the frame; In terms of light and shadow, the overall atmosphere leans toward soft diffuse light, with light filtering through gaps in the leaves forming mottled, jumping highlights on the shoulders, skirts, and umbrella surfaces. At the same time, deep and soft shadows are cast on the trunk and ground, with sharp contrasts of light and shadow that are not glaring, creating a warm, tranquil, and slightly mysterious dusk atmosphere; The color palette is dominated by vibrant orange-red, complemented by the elegant white-gray of kimono, the pale purple of paper umbrellas, and the golden brown of fallen leaves, creating an autumn scene full of Eastern classical charm. The colors are rich and full without being overly gaudy, presenting a visual experience that is both dreamy and authentic. The overall atmosphere is filled with a rich autumnal atmosphere, Zen charm, and the beauty of time accumulation. It combines the exquisite lighting texture of a studio with the subtle details of light and shadow changes in a real natural environment. It feels like a documentary photographed with amateur equipment yet full of professional aesthetics and artistic appeal. Every detail radiates a serene and far-reaching vitality, inviting pause and gaze, feeling the poetic and lonely beauty of the changing seasons.",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
          "is_user_plan": false,
