        {
          "id": "krea2-2ad310042bca5135f9a4ce51",
          "alias": "单女棕围巾雪地忧伤站立持伞",
          "prompt": "A woman dressed in light blue Hanfu stands sideways, her expression calm yet slightly melancholic, as if lost in her own thoughts. Her right hand gently grips the handle of an off-white oil-paper umbrella. The umbrella is half-open, presenting a classical ink landscape pattern. The ribs are clearly visible, and red tassels adorn the top, adding a splash of color to the elegant scene. On her shoulders is a thick brown fur shawl, with a delicate and fluffy texture, with edges naturally hanging down, creating a material contrast with the lightweight Hanfu. The composition centers on the figure occupying the center-left position of the composition. The oil-paper umbrella extends diagonally from the upper left corner to the lower right, forming a diagonal line to guide the visuals. The background is blurred, presenting a hazy gray-green tone. The outdoor environment is faintly shrouded in rain and mist, with fine white particles scattered in the air, simulating snowflakes or raindrops to create a cool and moist atmosphere. The overall lighting is soft and even, with scattered light from above, creating rich layers of light and shadow. The details of clothing folds and fur textures are distinct, with cool tones predominantly intertwined with blue, gray, white, and brown. A harmonious and unified visual impression is formed, with the painting filled with Eastern classical aesthetics, combining the gentle elegance of traditional attire with the tranquil solitude of winter snowy scenes. The composition is compact and full of tension, extending to the textured details of the fur shawl, forming a complete narrative chain. The overall atmosphere is serene and far-reaching, poetic and picturesque, as if frozen in a poetic moment, possessing strong artistic appeal and emotional depth",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
          "is_user_plan": false,
          "created_at": "2026-09-17T13:54:20.693554",
