        {
          "id": "krea2-b9895cf9850d28c4d085f3c0",
          "alias": "单女米围巾公寓微笑阅读",
          "prompt": "She slightly tilts her head up to look at the camera, her hands gently holding a thick beige plush scarf, as if hiding a smile or seeking warmth in the cold. The soft and fluffy texture of the scarf contrasts with her fair skin. She wears a loose light gray coat made of wool or wool, with natural pleats and drape, making her look both warm and fashionable. Her fingers are long and her nails are neatly trimmed. Painted with light pink nail polish, hands naturally relaxed, creating an effortless elegance that dominates the scene. In the background is a coffee shop called \"Brewbar,\" with white letters \"COFFEE TO GO\" and \"COFFEE AND BEANS\" written on the glass window. The handwriting is simple AND modern, reflecting blurred images of the sky AND surrounding buildings. Inside the window, you can faintly see coffee machines, paper cups, AND some bottled beverages, creating a real sense of life. On the right side is a black, wooden-framed signboard with white letters reading \"COFFEE AND BEANS LEAVES COFFEE APARTMENT,\" adding realism AND narrative value to the scene. The entire scene uses shallow depth of field filming, with a soft background blur that highlights the subject's delicate expressions and emotional expression. The light comes from natural light. Perhaps the scattered light from cloudy days or evening is on the cool side, mainly gray-blue, off-white, and light brown, creating a tranquil and slightly melancholic atmosphere. Warm yellow lights shine through the store, creating a soft halo on the glass, subtly contrasting with the cool tones and enhancing the layering of the image. The light and shadow are evenly distributed without strong shadows, details are clearly visible, and the overall atmosphere is quiet and poetic, like a street snapshot taken with everyday hobby equipment, preserving the authentic texture of life and the beauty of a moment. There are no obvious post-production traces in the image, presenting an unretouched natural state, as if capturing an ordinary yet touching urban corner, evoking brief pauses and inner monologues in urban life",
