          "id": "krea2-33bebb1f26e24e5c34f5517d",
          "alias": "单女露胸白连衣裙酒店忧伤站立注视",
          "prompt": "A young woman stands topless by the hotel window, her bare shoulders and delicate collarbones exposed, a soft white floral slip dress crumpled at her waist, the tiny pink blossoms barely visible against the pale fabric. Her black hair is swept up in a high bun secured by a dark clip, a few strands falling loosely against her cheek. Round metal-rimmed glasses frame her eyes, their lenses catching the dim indoor light, adding an air of intellectual mystery. Her right hand holds a glass of deep red wine, the liquid trembling gently, catching a warm glow. Her left hand grips a dark green wine bottle, its label blurred but textured. She stands slightly turned, hips tilted, one leg forward, relaxed yet charged with tension. Her gaze drifts toward the window, lips slightly parted, a mix of contemplation and languor. In the foreground, sheer white curtains ripple softly, their fine texture and gentle folds visible. To the right, a beige upholstered headboard with soft curves, the bed linens rumpled, hinting at a recent rest or the night to come. Her bare breasts are natural and full, the areolas faint, skin glowing under the warm side light. The composition places her at the golden ratio, focus on her face, hands, and the wine. Beyond, a vast floor-to-ceiling window frames a glittering city nightscape, distant skyscrapers outlined in warm yellow and white neon, traffic streaks forming dynamic light ribbons. The sky is deep blue fading to black. Indoor lighting is soft and warm, from a bedside lamp or hidden source, illuminating her silhouette and the details of the discarded dress, casting delicate shadows on walls and curtains. The window glass reflects the interior, creating a layered depth. Shot with a mid-range lens, slight wide-angle distortion, full-frame sensor, ISO 400, 1/60 sec, f/2.8, 50mm, shallow depth of field, background beautifully blurred. Color contrast between warm indoor light and cool outdoor blues enhances the visual impact. The style blends art photography with candid intimacy, as if a private moment captured by a professional camera—a story of urban night solitude, lonely beauty, and self-indulgent peace. The composition is tight yet not crowded, the visual loop guiding the eye from her gaze to the window, back to the wine glass, evoking a silent nocturnal sonata.",
