        {
          "id": "krea2-646cb24f2a629a0f25a86387",
          "alias": "单女绿外套街道叛逆站立脱衣",
          "prompt": "A young woman stands on a street corner in a Japanese city, her black hair long with straight bangs, her gaze locked on the camera—defiant, contemplative. She wears a military-green bomber jacket with brown faux-fur collar, unzipped to reveal her bare chest, the white high-neck top discarded. A red-and-black plaid scarf hangs loose around her neck. Below, a blue-gray plaid pleated micro-skirt barely covers her hips. Her hands slip into the jacket pockets, posture relaxed yet aloof. Strong sunlight floods the scene, casting sharp shadows. To the left, an orange awning edge; to the right, an ITO EN vending machine in blue and white, lettered \"OMOTENASHI\" and Japanese script. The backdrop is a typical urban Japanese street—mid-rise apartments, commercial buildings, pedestrians and cars, one passerby in a blue coat and mask moving left. Sky clear, deep blue, sunlight from upper left etching crisp shadows on ground and body. Composition centers her slightly right; foreground is her figure, midground the vending machine and street, background receding buildings. Perspective lines and verticals guide the eye to her. The orange awning's diagonal contrasts with the vending machine's geometric blue. Lighting is stark, warm sun against cool shadows, creating cinematic yet everyday street realism. Film-grain texture, saturated colors, as if shot on an old camera at 35mm, f/2.8, 1/125 sec, +0.7 EV compensation—a genuine winter afternoon moment. Colors blend olive, blue, orange, red—harmonious yet sharp. Her interaction with the environment feels natural, exuding urban independence and attitude. Details are rich: jacket stitching, scarf weave, skirt pleats, manhole cover, distant car reflections—all building a real, layered, story-driven street scene.",
